<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Brandin Podziemski on a Rookie Contract?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Podziemski is paid <strong>$5.68m</strong> because he was the 19th pick in 2023, and this is the last season of the rookie scale before his <strong>$110m</strong> extension starts.</p>
<ul>
<li>First-round salaries are fixed by slot, so his production over four seasons hasn’t moved the number by a dollar.</li>
<li>He rebounds at a rate almost no guard matches, which creates possessions and lets Golden State play smaller lineups without giving up the glass.</li>
<li>He passes well enough to run an offense in stretches, and that has kept him in the rotation through three seasons of a club with championship expectations.</li>
<li>Golden State exercised both club option years, which is the club saying it valued him above what the option cost.</li>
<li>The extension he signed on October 10 takes him past restricted free agency, which he would otherwise have reached next summer at 24.</li>
</ul>
<p>He goes into the new deal with four seasons of starts behind him.</p>

