<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/brandin-podziemski/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/brandin-podziemski/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Brandin Podziemski’s Salary in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Podziemski earns $5.68m in 2026-27, up from $3.69m last season and the last year of his rookie contract. He’s ninth on the Golden State payroll. His career earnings come to $16.24m across four seasons, which is the full value of the deal because he’s played every year of it with the club that drafted him. This season takes up 2.57% of Golden State’s $220.84m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Brandin Podziemski Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The rookie contract ends after this season, and the five-year, $110m extension he signed on October 10 takes over in 2027-28. The final season, 2031-32, is a mutual option."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Brandin Podziemski Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $5.68m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Brandin Podziemski’s Contract With the Warriors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Podziemski signed his rookie contract on July 3, 2023, four years and $16.24m, fully guaranteed. Golden State exercised the club options on both the third and fourth seasons, each a day before the deadline. On October 10, 2026 he signed a five-year extension worth $110m that runs from 2027-28 to 2031-32 and includes a trade bonus. The fifth season is a mutual option, so he could reach free agency in 2031 at 28 or in 2032 at 29."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is Brandin Podziemski’s Net Worth Today?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Podziemski’s net worth is estimated at around $6.5m, derived from his $16.24m in career earnings. Nobody publishes a figure for a player in his fourth season. Rookie contracts for picks in the late teens pay between $3m and $6m a year, so four seasons of it adds up to less than a single year of what the players above him on this roster earn. His $110m extension, which starts next season, is where the real money starts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Is Brandin Podziemski on a Rookie Contract?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Podziemski is paid $5.68m because he was the 19th pick in 2023, and this is the last season of the rookie scale before his $110m extension starts. He goes into the new deal with four seasons of starts behind him."}}]}</script>
